<title>USA: Federal Screw warns of prolonged GM strike.</title>
<headline>Federal Screw warns of prolonged GM strike.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Screw Works said Monday the Canadian Auto Workers strike against General Motors Corp may hurt the company's business.</p>
<p>For the first quarter ended September 30, Federal Screw reported earnings of $0.73 a share, compared with $0.46 in the same period the previous year.</p>
<p>&quot;A prolonged strike by the Canadian Auto Workers against General Motors will adversely affect our business,&quot; Federal Screw Works said in a statement. &quot;Despite this, we believe that the company will record another strong year.&quot;</p>
<p>The strike in Canada began on October 3.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
